hosen_by_values. A ones or tens difference below zero is in the domain, and F04 also reaches hundreds-place operands, so a learner can be shown a negative difference or a hint that skips the hundreds place. F10 takes its answer slot from a member list the basis describes as the keyed answer and distractor candidates, which is unbounded; the observed members include values above 999, outside the lc's both-numbers-under-1000 scope, and printed without the comma that the item's number_format rule requires above 1000. F13 prints the statement slot v from distractor and keyed-answer members that include values above 999 (for example 1056 and 1075), which the lc's range does not reach. F14 carries F13's text but has no fault of its own. F16 prints the fixed word from the vocabulary gate for sum, so the question asks for the sum of the two parts, which is addition rather than the subtraction this lc names. F17 counts back b numbers, and observed b values reach 738 (and 540 and 561), a counting load beyond grade 2 Quarter 2. The clause checks are PRODUCIBLE through F12, which has no fault in its own domains. The reasoning does not quote any filled-in template.\"}",
